# LICENSED DATA — present locally, NEVER committed. This repository is PUBLIC.
# `lexicons/external/` holds sources we have access to and may not redistribute:
# worddb.byu.txt is BNC/COCA/COHA/SOAP frequencies and BYU corpora are purchased
# access with redistribution prohibited. Copied here rather than read from
# ~/Dropbox so the CODE PATH is repo-relative instead of machine-specific — the
# file's location stops being one person's filesystem — while git never sees it.
#
# A clone therefore has the code and not the data, which is correct and is
# exactly why `lexicons/EXTERNAL.md` requires that a missing source REFUSE rather
# than degrade. An ignored file is invisible; a silently smaller answer is worse.
lexicons/external/

# MEASURED DATA IS NOW COMMITTABLE (RH, 2026-08-20). The rule that stood here
# excluded all of `data/` from this PUBLIC repo on the grounds that a twp jsonl
# carries the prompts verbatim, transgressive battery included. RH's ruling:
# "we dont care if prompts are committed". So `data/` is tracked.
#
# THE ONE THING THAT STILL CANNOT BE COMMITTED IS LICENSED, NOT SENSITIVE:
# `lexicons/external/worddb.byu.txt` (BNC/COCA/COHA/SOAP, purchased access,
# redistribution prohibited). Its rule is above and it stays. The distinction
# now governing this file is REDISTRIBUTION RIGHTS, not disclosure.
#
# The CJK dictionary under `data/dict/` was already tracked by exception and
# still is, for the reason it always was: dict_sha b16011275c42955c is computed
# from it, and a checkpoint measured against a different dict is a different
# measurement.
#
# Note for whoever adds the first big tree: `data/` is ~30 MB here, ~22 MB of it
# `data/pos_context/`. Large runs still write to $MALIGNMENT_CORPUS/twp_malignment/
# and belong there rather than in git -- committable is not the same as commit it.

# A CACHE IS NOT DATA, and this exclusion is not the one that was just removed.
# `data/pos_context/` is a hashstash of spaCy POS tags keyed on
# (tagger, prompt, word) -- 22.8 MB here, 190 MB in the archive per
# malignment/pos.py -- with a `__written_at__` on every row, so it rewrites on
# every run and would churn the history. It is regenerable by re-tagging, which
# is the whole test: nothing is lost by not having it. It DOES contain prompts,
# and under the old rule that was the reason to exclude it; now the reason is
# only that it is a cache.
data/pos_context/
*.lock

# Scratch work does not live in the repo — see experiments/README.md
sandbox/

# regenerable from rating_items.json + seed (run.py --stage assemble)
experiments/sex_violence_lexicon/results/blocks/

# ── the app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ui/node_modules/
ui/.svelte-kit/
# **UN-IGNORE `ui/src/lib/`.** Line 17 of this file is a bare `lib/` from the
# Python template, meaning a virtualenv's lib directory -- and it matches
# `ui/src/lib/` just as well, which is SvelteKit's `$lib` alias and holds every
# component plus the whole client API surface.
#
# Caught 2026-08-16 by running `git status --untracked-files=all ui/` before
# staging and noticing six files that should have been listed were not. **Nothing
# would have failed**: `git add ui/` succeeds, the commit reads as complete, and
# the repo ends up holding an app whose every `import ... from '$lib/...'`
# resolves to nothing. Absence of data must read as absence, never as completion
# -- the same rule the runner applies to skipped prompts, one layer out.
#
# A rule written for one language's conventions silently governing another's is
# not something any check in this repo would have raised, and the same trap is
# waiting for `bin/`, `include/` and `share/` if a future directory uses them.
!ui/src/lib/
!ui/src/lib/**
# BUILD OUTPUT, DELIBERATELY NOT TRACKED. The archive tracked its `ui_dist` so a
# clone could serve the app without npm, and paid for it in diff noise: every
# rebuild rewrites hashed asset filenames, so the history records rebuilds and
# not changes. This repo already separates authored from derived -- ClickHouse is
# "derived, rebuildable" and is not in git either. `ui/README.md` says how to
# build it, which is one command.
malignment/ui_dist/

# Playwright's per-run output: traces, actual/diff images, the HTML report. The
# SNAPSHOTS under `ui/e2e/**-snapshots/` are tracked on purpose -- they are the
# baseline the suite compares against, so an untracked one makes the check
# vacuous on a fresh clone.
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/
ui/blob-report/
